SecureScope — licensing scope
=============================

This repository contains BOTH original work and a vendored third-party
component, and they are NOT under the same license.

  * The MIT License below applies ONLY to the original code in this
    repository:

        firecrawl/                    CVE intelligence engine
        cve_scorer/                   CVE scoring / ensemble ranking
        incident_report_generator/    Incident report generation
        vulntracker-ui/               Next.js dashboard
        README.md, NOTICE, .gitattributes

  * The `opencve/` directory is a vendored and modified copy of OpenCVE
    and is NOT MIT licensed. It is governed by the Business Source
    License 1.1, whose full text is in `opencve/LICENSE`. See
    `opencve/NOTICE` and the root `NOTICE` file for details, including
    the Additional Use Grant and the 2030-01-13 Change Date after which
    it converts to Apache License 2.0.

  * `vulntracker-ui/components/ui/` contains components generated by the
    shadcn/ui CLI (MIT). See `NOTICE`.

Nothing in the MIT License below grants any rights in `opencve/`, and
nothing in it may be read as relicensing that directory.

